* The read phase of one operand of a two-operand loop: the statement ` branch C Q ( pop K F Q ) ` steps to its continuation ` Q ` either at the unchanged configuration (the operand is exhausted, the branch is taken) or with the head of stack ` K ` popped into the handler ` F ` .  Lean: ` OpA.read ` and ` OpB.read ` of TM/Arith.lean, whose ` exists v1 S1 ` are the class variables ` A' ` , ` D' ` and whose disjunction is ` OpA ` itself.  The continuation ` Q ` is a class variable, so one instance per operand assembles the read phase of ` addBody ` , ` subBody ` and ` cmpBody ` .

